<title>POLAND: Polish grain prices all rise in latest week.</title>
<headline>Polish grain prices all rise in latest week.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish wheat, rye and barley prices rose at last week's grain auctions, the Agriculture Ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>POLISH FARM AUCTION PRICES (AVERAGE)</p>
<p>  Product   week to June 21    previous week    yr/yr change</p>
<p>   Wheat	52.10 zl/q	  52.00 zl/q	 -20 pct</p>
<p>   Rye	  39.74 zl/q	  38.00 zl/q	 -34 pct</p>
<p>   Barley     46.74 zl/q	  46.00 zl/q	 -18 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: zl/q = zlotys per quintal.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom+48 22 653 9700</p>
